	(text "NETWORK  —  Network: RTL8211FD-CG gigabit PHY and ETH jack, LINK P and LINK Q raw LVDS ports  —  HW 0.1.0-proto.1" (at 40 20 0) (effects (font (size 4 4) (thickness 0.6)) (justify left)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 41.91) (end 444.5 198.12) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "932de8f2-88c4-a21c-8026-543b79487630"))
	(text "U30  gigabit PHY" (at 33.02 45.72 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "U30 is the Ethernet PHY: it turns the FPGA's RGMII bus (four data bits each way plus clock and control, 2.5 V, bank 16) into 1000Base-T signals on the ETH jack's four twisted pairs. The FPGA still needs a MAC; the PHY handles the line, link negotiation and the analog side. It runs\nfrom +3V3, takes its RGMII pad supply from +2V5 and makes its own 1.0 V core supply with an internal LDO (the FD variant, so no inductor). The capacitors here bypass those supplies (RTL8211F datasheet rev 1.7, Table 9)." (at 33.02 50.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 218.44) (end 510.54 280.67) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "861e0f36-7989-61f2-ad2e-53d3992a764e"))
	(text "PHY straps and LEDs" (at 33.02 222.25 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Resistors that configure U30 at reset and drive its LEDs. During reset the PHY reads the level on several output pins as configuration: PHY address 1, PLL kept running, 2 ns clock delays on both RGMII directions (so the FPGA needs none), and an external 2.5 V I/O supply (RTL8211F Tables 10 and 11). The same LED pins later drive\nthe jack's LEDs, whose polarity follows the strap (section 7.9, Figure 5). Also here: the reset pull-down that holds the PHY in reset until the FPGA is configured, the interrupt and MDIO pull-ups. Full table: ref/network.md." (at 33.02 227.33 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 300.99) (end 198.12 485.14) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "b0b2ae09-2ca7-05dd-1cf3-8384cc375f6d"))
	(text "ETH jack" (at 33.02 304.8 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "The Ethernet connector, with the 1000Base-T transformers and two LEDs built into the jack. The transformers\nisolate the cable from the board; the capacitor returns their centre taps to ground (ref/network.md)." (at 33.02 309.88 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 209.55 300.99) (end 378.46 367.03) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "0e3839aa-01f6-b9d6-3f72-6e27e75fc5e3"))
	(text "PHY clock" (at 212.09 304.8 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "The 25 MHz crystal U30 needs as its reference (RTL8211F Table 56: 25 MHz, +/-50 ppm all in). The two capacitors\nset the crystal's load; the 0 ohm resistor is a placeholder to limit crystal drive if measurement shows it needs\nit." (at 212.09 309.88 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 505.46) (end 313.69 598.17) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "82723487-d83e-d988-acdc-a1a7c269faf2"))
	(text "LINK P" (at 33.02 509.27 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "A board-to-board link port, not Ethernet. Four LVDS pairs from FPGA bank 16 go straight to an RJ45 so two boards can be cabled with shielded twisted pair: a clock and a data pair out, a clock\nand a data pair in. Cable LINK P of one board to LINK Q of the other, and power both boards before plugging in (ref/link-ports.md). The two arrays clamp ESD at the jack." (at 33.02 514.35 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 618.49) (end 313.69 707.39) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "a6496b4d-373a-c9d7-0183-1df12c4cb7fe"))
	(text "LINK Q" (at 33.02 622.3 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "The second link port, wired as the mirror of LINK P so a straight cable from a P to a Q connects outputs to inputs. Same rules: STP cable, power both boards first (ref/link-ports.md)." (at 33.02 627.38 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
